// M5-A3P-1003. Ch18 K07 "The Kite at night" (E, 3 min). act3_ch18.md §2 K07, §10 Q4: one short
// follow-up per camp pair the player saw (ch10..ch16_camp_talk); if none were seen, the generic deck scene.
// Kerrid stands at the stern rail throughout. Each follow-up is one exchange, never a recap of the camp.
title: ch18_night_aboard
location: ch18/kite
---
@camera K14
@music the_kite fade=3.0
@mark kerrid stern_rail walk
@wait 3.0
<<if not ($ch10_camp_talk or $ch11_camp_talk or $ch12_camp_talk or $ch13_camp_talk or $ch14_camp_talk or $ch15_camp_talk or $ch16_camp_talk)>>
    Toma [neutral]: Quiet up here. You can hear the lamps. #line:ch18_night_001
    Liss [neutral]: That's the engine. The lamps don't make a sound. #line:ch18_night_002
<<endif>>
<<if $ch10_camp_talk>>
    Rhen [neutral]: You said I'd know what it cost. #line:ch18_night_003
    Pell [neutral]: Now you do. I am sorry it was this. #line:ch18_night_004
<<endif>>
<<if $ch11_camp_talk>>
    Asha [tender]: You said glad was the word you would want. #line:ch18_night_005
    Pell [neutral]: It still is. #line:ch18_night_006
<<endif>>
<<if $ch12_camp_talk>>
    Ysolde [neutral]: The end of the road is further than you said. #line:ch18_night_007
    Toma [soft_smile]: I'm still walking it. #line:ch18_night_008
<<endif>>
<<if $ch13_camp_talk>>
    Asha [neutral]: Did you learn the difference? In the end? #line:ch18_night_009
    Ysolde [neutral]: Most days. #line:ch18_night_010
<<endif>>
<<if $ch14_camp_talk>>
    Rhen [neutral]: Do you still want it to cost them? #line:ch18_night_011
    Liss [sad]: It costs everyone. That was the part I didn't want. #line:ch18_night_012
<<endif>>
<<if $ch15_camp_talk>>
    Toma [neutral]: Bottom step's still yours? #line:ch18_night_013
    Kerrid [neutral]: Till I'm relieved. #line:ch18_night_014
<<endif>>
<<if $ch16_camp_talk>>
    Asha [soft_smile]: Still counting? #line:ch18_night_015
    Rhen [tender]: Every night. #line:ch18_night_016
<<endif>>
@wait 3.0
<<set $ch18_night_aboard = true>>
===
